\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Worst-channel artifact under 3~Hz stimulation (red) versus same-day unstimulated reference (grey dashed). (a) One second of raw LFP around the peak transient. (b) Recording folded at the 333~ms period showing cycle-wise median and unclipped interquartile range (25--75\% shaded). The flat fold demonstrates that slow transient decay, rather than a stable periodic waveform, dominates the distortion.}}{3}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:artifact3}{{2}{3}{Worst-channel artifact under 3~Hz stimulation (red) versus same-day unstimulated reference (grey dashed). (a) One second of raw LFP around the peak transient. (b) Recording folded at the 333~ms period showing cycle-wise median and unclipped interquartile range (25--75\% shaded). The flat fold demonstrates that slow transient decay, rather than a stable periodic waveform, dominates the distortion}{figure.caption.7}{}}
